  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/9f1f11fbb4e091305a6b414e74c3aec25b8d519670a1f3bd65f5bd4eb1bdcd68.png] \n\nGiven equation: 29 - 23 + 42 × 21 ÷ 2 = 10\n\nOption 1) - and ÷\n\nBy interchanging which two signs:\n\n⇒ __**29 ÷ 23**__ + 42 × 21 - 2 = 10\n\n⇒ 1.27 +__** 42 × 21**__ - 2 = 10\n\n⇒ __**1.27 + 882**__ - 2 = 10\n\n⇒ __**883.27 - 2**__ = 10\n\n⇒ 881.27 ≠ 10\n\nOption 2) + and ÷\n\nBy interchanging which two signs:\n\n⇒ 29 - __**23 ÷ 42 × 21**__ + 2 = 10\n\n⇒ __**29**__ - 11.5 __**+ 2**__ = 10\n\n⇒ __**31 - 11.5**__ = 10\n\n⇒ 19.5 ≠ 10\n\nOption 3) − and ×\n\nBy interchanging which two signs:\n\n⇒ 29 × 23 + 42 - __**21 ÷ 2**__ = 10\n\n⇒ __**29 × 23**__ + 42 - 10.5 = 10\n\n⇒__** 667 + 42**__ - 10.5 = 10\n\n⇒ __**709 - 10.5**__ = 10\n\n⇒ 698.5 ≠ 10\n\n**Option 4) ÷ and ×**\n\nBy interchanging which two signs:\n\n⇒ 29 - 23 + **__42 ÷ 21__** × 2 = 10\n\n⇒ 29 - 23 + __**2 × 2**__ = 10\n\n⇒ __**29**__ - 23 __**+ 4**__ = 10\n\n⇒ __**33 - 23**__ = 10\n\n⇒** 10 = 10**\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"**÷ and ×**\".",
